# Per-job runtime output (apps/protection-svc/out/<jobId>/...), not
# checked in -- purely generated per protect() call.
/out/

# ml-engine/out/ is mostly local scratch (manual test runs' cloaked.png
# etc.) EXCEPT style_target.png, which orchestrate.py's protect() falls
# back to as the *default* style target for every real upload that
# doesn't pass its own styleTargetUri (i.e. every real upload today --
# see remote_gpu.py's own comment: "the fixed default asset is what
# every real protect() job actually compared against"). That makes it a
# required source asset, not a job artifact, even though it lives in
# this otherwise-ignored directory -- found the hard way when the
# Docker image built without it and every protect() job failed with
# "No such file or directory: '.../ml-engine/out/style_target.png'".
/ml-engine/out/*
!/ml-engine/out/style_target.png
